Intercepting Proxy Basics
==========================================

--- LAUNCHING BURP ---
burpsuite &                          # or: Applications > 03 - Web Application Analysis > burpsuite
   Temporary project -> Use Burp defaults -> Start Burp

--- BROWSER SETUP ---
Proxy tab -> "Open Browser"            # Burp's own pre-configured browser, easiest option
   -- OR, for your regular Firefox --
Firefox Settings -> Network Settings -> Manual proxy configuration
   HTTP Proxy: 127.0.0.1   Port: 8080   [x] Also use this proxy for HTTPS
Visit http://burp in the proxied browser to install Burp's CA cert (needed for HTTPS later)

--- THE PROXY TAB ---
Intercept tab           shows ONE request at a time, paused, waiting for Forward/Drop
  Forward                 let this one request through unchanged
  Drop                     kill this request, nothing reaches the server
  (edit the raw request text directly before forwarding - this is the core "intercept and modify" workflow)
HTTP history tab         a log of EVERY request/response that passed through, intercepted or not

--- REPEATER ---
Right-click any request (in history or while intercepted) -> "Send to Repeater"
  Edit anything in the request, click Send, see the response - repeat as many times as needed,
  without touching the browser at all. The main tool for "let me just try this one variation."

